<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guizhou</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guizhou is a mountainous province of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, with Guiyang as its capital. Home to many non-Han peoples such as the Miao, Buyei and Dong, it lay in ancient times within the lands of Yelang and other south-western kingdoms. It became a regular province under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a> in 1413 and remains one of China's poorer regions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guizhou.jpg" alt="Guizhou" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Huangdan2060 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huangguoshu_Waterfall_in_October_2020,_Picture12.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
